      "worked": "If $x\\ge1$, then $|x-1|=x-1$ and $2x-1\\ge1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\left|x-\\left|x+|x-1|\\right|\\right| &= |x-(2x-1)|\\\\\n\\left|x-\\left|x+|x-1|\\right|\\right| &= |1-x|\\\\\n\\left|x-\\left|x+|x-1|\\right|\\right| &= |x-1|.\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nIf $x<1$, then $|x-1|=1-x$ and $x+|x-1|=1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\left|x-\\left|x+|x-1|\\right|\\right| &= \\left|x-|1|\\right|\\\\\n\\left|x-\\left|x+|x-1|\\right|\\right| &= |x-1|.\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe two cases cover every real $x$, so the identity holds for all real $x$.",
